// What a ruin has instead of a lock.
//
// Wardens are the counterweight to the cling rule. `DECISIONS.md` §11
// makes a creature's grip count down only while the tower is actually
// striding, so "keep the legs moving" is a real, free answer to a wave
// — and berthing is the one time the tower cannot walk away, not
// because a rule forbids it but because walking away is what ends the
// salvage. The escape hatch closes itself. A warden's grip never runs
// out while you keep working, and the moment you decide the scrap is
// not worth it you start walking and it does.
//
// Tone: this is a creature defending the place it lives, roused by the
// tower taking the place apart. It is not guarding treasure.
#![enable(implicit_some)]
EnemyDef(
    id: "enemy.feral_warden",
    name: "Feral Warden",
    glyph: "🦂",
    // The toughest thing in the pack, by half again over a root-borer
    // (225). A dart battery needs 800 ticks and 20 darts to put one
    // down — 300 hp against 15 damage every 40 ticks — and takes about
    // 160 damage doing it, roughly 16 poles to mend. One ruin is one
    // real fight.
    hp: 300,
    // Slower even than a root-borer (15... 20 here is a shade above it,
    // and well under half the tower's own 60). It does not need to
    // hurry: you are the one who stopped.
    speed_paces_per_100_ticks: 20,
    damage: 12,
    attack_ticks: 60,
    // The longest grip in the pack by twice over: 2,400 ticks is 80
    // seconds of *walking* to shake one you have decided to leave. The
    // price of changing your mind about a berth.
    cling_ticks: 2400,
    approach: Ground,
    // 30, against warden_threat_per_100_salvage (120): a 25-unit ruin
    // rouses one warden and a 50-unit ruin rouses two. The payout and
    // the price are the same number, which is the whole point.
    threat: 30,
    // Not summoned by attention. A warden is summoned by berthing, so
    // it is excluded from the ordinary provocation-driven pool
    // explicitly rather than fenced off with an out-of-range
    // min_provocation, which would be a number pretending to be a rule.
    wave_eligible: false,
)
